xxm values need to be aligned by 16 bytes for you to use a 4 value struct
Every single precision float is 4 bytes.

const char* in fasm do not need [] because they are values passed directly
[] would dereference the address,
the function DrawText(const char* title) expects an address so no []

order of linux abi V:
rdi, rsi, rdx, rcx, r8, r9, r10, r11

Variadic function:
   A function that takes a variable number of arguements like printf and sprintf.
   Each one requires 16 byte alignment, for example:
updateGame:
.update_card_number:
   sub rsp, 8
   lea rdi, [text.message]
   lea rsi, [fmt_int]
   mov edx, [card_number]
   xor eax, eax
   call sprintf 
   add rsp, 8
   
   Every function call in fasm requires 8 bytes so this variadic function needs
   rsp to be 16-byte aligned before usage
